{
  "an11.9:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 11.9 ",
  "an11.9:0.2": "1. Dependence ",
  "an11.9:0.3": "With Sandha ",
  "an11.9:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying at Ñātika in the brick house. ",
  "an11.9:1.2": "Then Venerable Sandha went up to the Buddha, bowed, and sat down to one side. The Buddha said to him: ",
  "an11.9:2.1": "“Sandha, meditate like a thoroughbred, ",
  "an11.9:2.2": "not like a wild colt. ",
  "an11.9:2.3": "And how does a wild colt meditate? ",
  "an11.9:2.4": "A wild colt, tied up by the feeding trough, meditates: ‘Fodder, fodder!’ ",
  "an11.9:2.5": "Why is that? ",
  "an11.9:2.6": "Because it doesn’t occur to the wild colt tied up by the feeding trough: ",
  "an11.9:2.7": "‘What task will the horse trainer have me do today? How should I respond?’ ",
  "an11.9:2.8": "Tied up by the feeding trough they just meditate: ‘Fodder, fodder!’ ",
  "an11.9:2.9": "In the same way, take a certain wild person who has gone to the forest, the root of a tree, or an empty hut. Their heart is overcome and mired in sensual desire, and they don’t truly understand the escape from sensual desire that has arisen. ",
  "an11.9:2.10": "Harboring sensual desire within they meditate and concentrate and contemplate and ruminate. ",
  "an11.9:2.11": "Their heart is overcome by ill will … ",
  "an11.9:2.12": "dullness and drowsiness … ",
  "an11.9:2.13": "restlessness and remorse … ",
  "an11.9:2.14": "doubt … ",
  "an11.9:2.15": "Harboring doubt within they meditate and concentrate a